WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 32 Leader Video
Unit 8, Lesson 4: Challenges

1
00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.630
All right, you did it.

2
00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:13.630
Final week, final lesson of this incredible year,

3
00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:17.630
studying apologetics, preparing your students

4
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:21.870
to be one step closer, to be entirely confident,

5
00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.310
to walk across the stage of graduation,

6
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.930
and to engage their culture with the truth of the gospel.

7
00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:32.510
I can't express how excited I am

8
00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:35.990
to hear the stories of our students

9
00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.710
and what they've been able to experience,

10
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.350
and the stories of students who started off

11
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.190
with this skepticism in doubt

12
00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:49.030
and have been brought along into committed followers of Christ,

13
00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.750
proclaiming the gospel far beyond the walls

14
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.790
of your youth group.

15
00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:56.230
So this is excited, I'm excited, I hope you're excited.

16
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:58.110
There's just a couple of quick things

17
00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.910
that I wanna bring to your attention

18
00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.310
and talk through as you kind of prepare.

19
00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.510
I hope, first and foremost,

20
00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:08.470
I hope you are preparing to celebrate.

21
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:11.990
This has been a, probably one of some of the most difficult

22
00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:13.310
topics that some of your students

23
00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.590
have ever dealt with in church studying,

24
00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:19.590
and that's awesome, that makes me very, very excited.

25
00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.150
So I'll take the time to celebrate.

26
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.310
But the second thing is,

27
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.350
is take some time to do an inventory.

28
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.870
Go back, when you first started talking,

29
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.090
go back to where your students were.

30
00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.250
Have your students go back to where they were,

31
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.950
and invite them to think through,

32
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:37.910
like, what was I thinking back,

33
00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:38.870
go back to their notes,

34
00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.270
and what were you thinking in lesson 1.1

35
00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.190
versus how you're thinking now?

36
00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:47.030
When the concept of apologetics was introduced

37
00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.750
and the questions that you had

38
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.950
way back in the beginning,

39
00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.710
have those questions been answered now?

40
00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.590
What further questions do you have?

41
00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:56.030
Where do we go from here?

42
00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.070
How do we continue to move on?

43
00:01:58.110 --> 00:01:59.730
For your seniors.

44
00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.590
Ask them if they feel like they're ready.

45
00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:04.910
And if they're not,

46
00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.510
maybe ask them what you can do to help them

47
00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.390
further be ready for the next step,

48
00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:11.470
the next step in their lives,

49
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.310
whether it be military, whether it be college,

50
00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.190
whether it be gap year, whatever it is,

51
00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.230
what is next for them?

52
00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.350
The next thing is success and failures.

53
00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:24.710
For your storyteller,

54
00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.670
you want someone that can tell a great story

55
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:30.430
about sharing the truth.

56
00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.070
But keep this in mind.

57
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:35.710
You don't necessarily want to have somebody

58
00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:40.710
who successfully shared the gospel every time.

59
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.270
Students are gonna need to see

60
00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.510
some examples of sort of falling flat on their face

61
00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:48.630
because they're probably going to,

62
00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.110
and that's okay, and maybe that's a good thing

63
00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.590
because you learn a lot more generally

64
00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.070
from failure than you do from successes.

65
00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.230
So have somebody that can express both sides,

66
00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:02.230
especially if you can find somebody that failed,

67
00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:05.870
learn from their failure and move down to some success.

68
00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.270
Keep in mind and remind your students time and again

69
00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:14.070
that it's not us who does the saving.

70
00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.590
It is God's job.

71
00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.990
I have this analogy I've often given students

72
00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.990
and they're all gonna be in different places

73
00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:24.910
and God's gonna have all different kinds of roles.

74
00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:28.830
Some water, some plant, but it's God who causes the growth.

75
00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:32.670
And I often talk about the wide range of jobs

76
00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.110
from excavation to tree shaking.

77
00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.790
I have this pastor friend of mine

78
00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.790
that I call him a tree shaker

79
00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.550
because he's one of those guys that is just so eloquent

80
00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:48.550
and so good at talking about the gospel

81
00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:50.830
that I think he can just say bless you

82
00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.510
and people come to faith in Jesus.

83
00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:53.670
He's just so good.

84
00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.670
God has just gifted him in amazing ways.

85
00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.110
So I call him a tree shaker, right?

86
00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.230
He just walks up to the tree that has been just,

87
00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.830
you know, ripened by a bunch of work

88
00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.390
from a bunch of other people

89
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.510
and he just gets up there and shakes that tree

90
00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.030
and the fruit just falls.

91
00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:14.150
And that may be the giftings of some of your students,

92
00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.590
but that's not necessarily the gifting

93
00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:17.310
of all of your students.

94
00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:19.310
I typically call myself an excavator.

95
00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:21.110
I'm the guy that just messes people up

96
00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.590
and gets the land ready to be planted

97
00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:26.510
and gets them all confused and thinking

98
00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:28.950
and gets people ready to hear truth

99
00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.990
and understand what truth is.

100
00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.950
It could be all over the map.

101
00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.910
So just remember to encourage your students

102
00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.710
that wherever they are on that spectrum

103
00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.350
to be faithful to the gifts and talents

104
00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.950
that God has given them,

105
00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.630
that they're gonna face some challenges.

106
00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:44.790
They're gonna face questions

107
00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.990
that they don't have answers to all the time.

108
00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.630
They're gonna have to seek them out.

109
00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:50.150
They're gonna have awesome success

110
00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.990
and they're gonna get the thrill

111
00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.590
of leading someone to know Christ.

112
00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:57.070
And remember, we continue to pray for you.

113
00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:58.910
We continue to work really hard here

114
00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:00.550
back at the home office to provide you

115
00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:02.230
with the best possible resources

116
00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:03.830
for you to disciple your students.

117
00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.830
Like I said, we would love to hear your stories.

118
00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.750
We would love to hear how this study

119
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:10.670
has impacted you and impacted your students.

120
00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.150
Share them on Facebook,

121
00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:14.230
share them on Twitter and Instagram.

122
00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.910
Give us an email, give us a phone call,

123
00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:17.950
whatever it takes,

124
00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.190
let us know how this study has impacted you

125
00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.590
and impacted your students in your ministry.

